course: dictionary
lesson: 14425
title: Overspend: spending more than planned
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To overspend means to spend more money than you have, or more than you planned to spend. A budget is a plan for how much money you can spend, so an overspend means you went over that limit.
explain: «Mia had five pounds for the fair, but she spent six pounds on snacks and rides.» Mia overspent by one pound. Check the numbers: if you spent more than you had or planned, you overspent.
explain: Overspend can also be a noun. «The school reported an overspend of £200 on the new roof.» In the news, this tells the reader that the money went over the limit.
fact: Overspend is a verb and a noun: you can overspend, or there can be an overspend.
fact: «Overspend» means to spend more money than you have or than you planned.
fact: A budget is a plan for how much money you can spend.
fact: An overspend is the amount spent above the plan or budget.
fact: A quick check: ask, "Did I spend more than I had or planned?" If yes, you overspent.
exercise: «Sam had £10 pocket money but spent £14 at the shop.» What did Sam do? | Saved some money | Lost his wallet | *Overspent | Gave money away
exercise: «The party budget was £50, but the party cost £62.» What is the overspend? | *£12 | £50 | £112
exercise: Yesterday, Ali ___ his pocket money on sweets. Choose the right word. | overspending | *overspent | overspends
test: «The council's overspend on the new road was big news.» What does overspend mean in this sentence? | Built the road quickly | *Spent more than the planned amount | Saved money on the road | Gave the road a new name
test: Which sentence uses overspend as a noun? | Let us overspend tonight | *The hospital reported an overspend of one million pounds | Mum will overspend the budget | We overspent our pocket money
exam: Jayden has a £20 budget for a day out and spends £26. Which word describes this? | He saved money | He won money | *He overspent
